% =====================================================================================
% Bibliography for "Protecting the Router Is Necessary but Not Sufficient".
%
% PROVENANCE OF THIS FILE
% Every arXiv identifier below was resolved against the live arXiv API before being
% written here, and the author lists are the ones arXiv returned. Nothing in this file
% was reconstructed from memory. If you add an entry, resolve it first.
%
% -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% READ THIS BEFORE EDITING: two DISTINCT papers our internal notes once conflated
% -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% An earlier draft of OVERVIEW.md claimed that the proposal's "Anonymous (2026)" entry
% and the "Fang & Huang" paper were the same work. They are NOT. They are two separate
% submissions with different theses, and both are cited here separately:
%
%   routequant2026   "Beyond Freezing the Router: Rank-Aligned Post-Training
%                     Quantization for Mixture-of-Experts Models"
%                    -> STILL ANONYMOUS, under review. This is the proposal's
%                       "Anonymous (2026)". Thesis: a full-precision router is
%                       INSUFFICIENT, because expert-output quantization error still
%                       shifts the next layer's router logits. Quantizes the router and
%                       corrects with Rank-Aware Jaccard Loss + Gap Hinge Loss.
%                    -> DO NOT invent authors for this entry.
%
%   fang2026router   "Router Choice Matters: Rank-Aware Post-Training Quantization for
%                     MoE Models", Yi-Zeng Fang and Juinn-Dar Huang.
%                    -> WITHDRAWN ICLR 2026 submission. This is the real "Fang & Huang",
%                       and it is the source of the near-neighbour rank-flip finding
%                       (most routing errors are rank flips around the top-k boundary).
%
% Also note: the proposal cited VSRAQ as "Park et al. (2026)". That attribution is
% CORRECT -- arXiv confirms the first author is Hancheol Park.
%
% VERIFICATION STATUS OF THE NON-arXiv ENTRIES
% OpenReview's API returns HTTP 403 to unauthenticated clients and its public forum
% pages sit behind a browser check, so routequant2026, fang2026router and sramoe could
% not be machine-verified from this machine. Their metadata is as supplied in our
% verified research notes. Open each forum URL in a browser and confirm before
% submitting. sramoe additionally has no forum ID recorded -- see its TODO.
% =====================================================================================


